{
  "_createdAt": "2026-04-27T18:26:19Z",
  "_id": "wp-post-136702-en",
  "_rev": "dJ4ZpMyfIFtQ0D7lyxhaYB",
  "_type": "article",
  "_updatedAt": "2026-07-05T16:13:04Z",
  "author": {
    "_ref": "author-legacy-archive",
    "_type": "reference"
  },
  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "000000000001",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "t98ud894h0ia",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "This question needs less a short answer than a correct splitting. For people travelling "
        },
        {
          "_key": "9cytxcedk53v",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "9frk58sfvvlt"
          ],
          "text": "Cairo"
        },
        {
          "_key": "rnfwfv30t12t",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "afxnpzq9g0o9",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "gi0anjjqozj3"
          ],
          "text": "Giza"
        },
        {
          "_key": "6qj7p4n4cyy3",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "dnllswgiwdge",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "6htf8te4b1kt"
          ],
          "text": "Luxor"
        },
        {
          "_key": "fsc7g80ojrp7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "3ilm1xkau67w",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "bvc25dheojqa"
          ],
          "text": "Aswan"
        },
        {
          "_key": "tq60rle8s2k1",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", a Nile cruise, and Red Sea resorts vs. people thinking about North Sinai or near the Libyan border, the character of risk is completely different in the same country."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "9frk58sfvvlt",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-83284",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "gi0anjjqozj3",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58854",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "6htf8te4b1kt",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58877",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "bvc25dheojqa",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58758",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000003",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000002",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Limited to standard tourist routes, Egypt is a country many travellers realistically travel. In 2025, Egypt received around 19 million travellers, with tourism infrastructure widely operating. Airports, hotels, guides, drivers, Nile cruises, and Red Sea resorts are used to handling foreign travellers."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000005",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000004",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "But talking about Egypt as a whole at one safety level is dangerous. There are areas to avoid. Situations to watch around political expression and photography. Scams and persistent touts in cities. For women travelling alone, preparation for unwanted attention and harassment is needed."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000007",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000006",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "So Egypt is not \"a country to be afraid of.\" It is also not \"a country to move through without knowing anything.\""
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000009",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000008",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Think by region"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The first thing to look at on an Egypt trip is not the country, but the map."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "veeb9wgc4gxo",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Most travellers visit Cairo and Giza, Luxor and Aswan, the Nile cruise, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "ik3hwom67v3l",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "wdxrp1b0e7ya"
          ],
          "text": "Hurghada"
        },
        {
          "_key": "cnwv9oq6n7xd",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "9jeywif7lkr2",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "8ql0xps50txd"
          ],
          "text": "Marsa Alam"
        },
        {
          "_key": "2k7cyqtfxw86",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", and Sharm el-Sheikh. This range has organised reception for visitors and is realistic to travel."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "wdxrp1b0e7ya",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58859",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "8ql0xps50txd",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58885",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "North Sinai is different. Many governments advise against travel to North Sinai. Areas close to the Libyan border, parts of the Western Desert, and border zones are not places to consider as extensions of ordinary tourist travel."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000011",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0mnkhwvyhnhj",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "South Sinai is considered separately from North Sinai. Sharm el-Sheikh, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "7m0hp7a83po6",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "itpebl27e7xd"
          ],
          "text": "Dahab"
        },
        {
          "_key": "1e9mv88a93iu",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", and St. Catherine are areas travellers visit; inland Sinai and road transfers need confirmation by season and security. For St. Catherine especially, premise on trusted arrangements and current local information."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "itpebl27e7xd",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-59436",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000013",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000012",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Cairo and Giza"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000015",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000014",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The most common problem travellers meet in Cairo is not violent crime."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000017",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "aj64h0q1i4c8",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "It is traffic chaos, persistent touts, overcharging, fake guides, and being led to tourist-oriented shops. Around the Giza pyramids, in "
        },
        {
          "_key": "x2anvscykeaz",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "l2mjkey3m8z6"
          ],
          "text": "Khan el-Khalili"
        },
        {
          "_key": "4xmabz05c9mi",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", and on arrival from the airport, the pressure can feel high for first-timers."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l2mjkey3m8z6",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.cairo.khan-el-khalili",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000019",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000018",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "This is less danger than the tiring kind of risk. Arrange car and guide in advance. Confirm fares before boarding. Don't accept guidance you didn't ask for. Decline briefly and clearly. Those four alone help a lot."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "At Cairo's larger hotels, museums, and major sites, security is visible. Reassuring, and also a sign of Egypt's national emphasis on tourism."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For women travelling alone, see Cairo a little more realistically. Verbal harassment, stares, and unwanted contact in crowded places can happen. Clothing doesn't avoid this completely, but covering shoulders and knees, avoiding quiet late-night streets, and moving by ride-hailing or trusted car lower the load."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Luxor, Aswan, Nile cruise"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000021",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000020",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Luxor and Aswan are relatively easy cities to move through."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000023",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000022",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Luxor has many travellers, and so more touts. At temple entrances, ferry landings, and parts of the west bank, people may approach you. Aswan is generally a little calmer; in souks and at boat landings the same exchanges happen."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000025",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "y3m1woquhcn7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The Nile cruise is one of Egypt's most established tourist corridors. The Luxor-"
        },
        {
          "_key": "etrfbhp1t7yl",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "y5gk54zuaa6n"
          ],
          "text": "Edfu"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gylj23aral1v",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "-"
        },
        {
          "_key": "ad2d9e4evkxg",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "k9vr7krcq9uj"
          ],
          "text": "Kom Ombo"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gpzskff8d6s5",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "-Aswan route has been operated long, with established flows for ships, guides, and drivers. For first travellers to Egypt who want to lower the load of transfers, this corridor is useful."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "y5gk54zuaa6n",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58841",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "k9vr7krcq9uj",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58875",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000027",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "ss8ddb1u5yig",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Itineraries that cover Middle Egypt by long road are what to watch. Minya, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "2qsnnhu8f796",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "iyvcmorqc876"
          ],
          "text": "Asyut"
        },
        {
          "_key": "a59hudm1hcmw",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "8p2v99x0p7vn",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "v8le94ds8cq1"
          ],
          "text": "Sohag"
        },
        {
          "_key": "pf3d2yntgyyn",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " area hold important sites, but tourist infrastructure is not as thick as in Luxor or Aswan. Move with arrangements that know the local situation, rather than organising loosely on your own."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "iyvcmorqc876",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58764",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "v8le94ds8cq1",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58937",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000029",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000028",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Red Sea"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "apkno42m5a7c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In Red Sea resorts like Hurghada, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "m20j4ifz6azf",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "58auetb7jghp"
          ],
          "text": "El Gouna"
        },
        {
          "_key": "u7y333c2wtbz",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", Soma Bay, Marsa Alam, and Sharm el-Sheikh, the centre of safety isn't town walking — it's water and transfers."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "58auetb7jghp",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58740",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Hotels and dive centres are used to foreign travellers. At larger resorts, even first travellers are relatively easy. The sea isn't a managed pool. Current, wind, boats, depth, coral, dive certification and experience all play in."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Even snorkelling, stay inside marked areas. For diving, use reputable centres. Don't go to sites beyond your certification or experience. The real safety on the Red Sea sits in these basics."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000031",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000030",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "If heading into town, don't walk with resort mentality. Avoid going to local shopping streets in swimwear, and treat transport and fares with the same care as in Cairo."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000033",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000032",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Scams and touts"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000035",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000034",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The most common unpleasant experience on an Egypt trip is less scam than pressured tourist commerce."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000037",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000036",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "\"It's closed here.\" \"Tickets are this way.\" \"Free guidance.\" \"I'll take your photo.\" \"This camel is cheap.\" Most of these calls lead to a fee or a shop in the end."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000039",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000038",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The most effective response is not to laugh and brush off vaguely. Decline briefly and leave the spot. Set prices first. Confirm official tickets at official windows or the official site. For guide or car, use someone selected in advance, not someone who suddenly approaches you on the spot."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "This doesn't mean Egyptians are unkind. In ordinary shops, hotels, family restaurants, on trains and the roadside, many will help. Around tourist site entrances, an economy that tries to extract maximum from visitors layers on top. Distinguishing matters."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Politics, photography, law"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In Egypt, political topics and photography need care."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000041",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000040",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Don't photograph military facilities, police stations, checkpoints, bridges, government buildings, or security forces. Not a light manners issue — it can lead to detention or questioning. If there are demonstrations or political gatherings, don't go near and don't photograph."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000043",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000042",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Be careful with social media too. Within usual sightseeing, problems are uncommon; posting strong criticism of the political system or security agencies while inside Egypt is an unnecessary risk."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000045",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000044",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For LGBT travellers, Egypt is a country where legal and social caution are needed. There is no simple law explicitly banning same-sex relations as such, but enforcement has occurred through public-morality frameworks. Care is needed with public affection and app use."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000047",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000046",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Health and transfer safety"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000049",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000048",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For most travellers, what actually causes problems is water, food, and heat."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Don't drink tap water; use bottled. In hot seasons in Luxor and Aswan, see sites in the morning and rest at midday. Hat, sunscreen, water, salt, breaks are not luxuries in summer Upper Egypt."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Stomach issues are common. Eating from stalls or small places isn't bad in itself; be careful with things sitting hot for long, things possibly washed in raw water, and ice."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Don't underestimate traffic. Cairo's roads are chaotic; even crossing takes practice. On long road transfers, avoid night driving and use trusted drivers and vehicles."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000051",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000050",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Confirm before going"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000053",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000052",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Always check your own country's travel advisory before going."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000055",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000054",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For Japanese travellers, MOFA's Overseas Travel Safety site and \"Tabi-Resi.\" UK FCDO, US State Department, Australia Smartraveller. These show not only country-level but region-level risk."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000057",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000056",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Don't judge only on a tour operator's or hotel's \"it's fine.\" Equally, don't decide on one frightening anecdote on social media. Official information, the practical sense of in-country handlers, and your own itinerary — combine those three to judge realistically."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000059",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000058",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In sum"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt is a country many travellers can travel safely."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "That doesn't mean \"equally safe everywhere.\" Avoid North Sinai and border zones. Understand tourist commercial pressure at Giza and markets. For women alone, hold a little margin in transfer and clothing. Avoid political photos and statements. Watch heat and water."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Hold these basics and Egypt isn't a country to fear — it is a country to receive densely."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000061",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000060",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Safety isn't believing nothing will happen."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000063",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000062",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "It is knowing where what tends to happen and being able to move calmly with that knowledge."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    }
  ],
